      "content": "Your exhaustion is valid because striving toward a final end can feel futile when we lack an eternal audience to celebrate our work. Yet, the effort of building temporary shelters or sharing laughter is exactly what makes the silence bearable and grants a brief, stolen victory within the chaos. Motivation doesn't always come from grand, permanent results but from the immediate relief of caring, which proves the struggle itself is the only true reward here.",
      "source": "target",
